# Python Port Plan — Step 00 · Configuration

## Purpose

Port `week1_baseline/ruby/00_config` (the `Boukensha::Config` step) to Python,
producing a `week1_baseline/python/00_config` package that is behaviourally
equivalent to the Ruby one: same config-dir resolution, same `settings.yaml`
schema, same task/prompt-resolution rules, same example output.

This is the first of what should become a series of
`docs/plans/python_port/<step>` plans — one per numbered baseline step — as
the Ruby line advances (`01_*`, `02_*`, …) and each gets ported in turn.
`mud_manager` (the Ruby telnet-session gem under `week0_explore/`) is **out of
scope** here — it hasn't been folded into a numbered `week1_baseline` step yet,
so it has no Ruby "spec" to port against. It will get its own plan once it
lands there.

